WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:05.170
Alex Garland's Annihilation might be the prettiest
end-of-the-world movie you'll ever see.

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:09.340
Based on the novel of the same name by Jeff
VanderMeer, the movie tells the story of a

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:13.820
group of scientists venturing into a strange
quarantined zone called the Shimmer.

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:17.910
Inside, they encounter a surreal world that
seems to be remixing itself, and everything

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:18.910
in it.

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:22.490
The film juggles some heavy themes and has
a lot going on in its narrative, so by the

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:25.410
time it ends, it's a little difficult to unpack.

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:27.980
Let's break down the ending of Annihilation.

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:30.030
From a galaxy far away

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:33.020
The film's primary question is: "What is the
Shimmer?"

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:37.020
The film's opening shots show some sort of
interstellar object careening through Earth's

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:40.870
atmosphere and crashing into a lighthouse,
which becomes the prime destination for the

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:45.600
research and military expeditions into Area
X, which is what the land surrounding the

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.079
Shimmer comes to be known as.

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:49.660
The Shimmer, as it turns out, is some sort
of alien force.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:54.899
It's either a thinking, living, breathing
thing, or a kind of celestial cancer, replicating

00:00:54.899 --> 00:00:55.899
itself unconsciously.

00:00:55.899 --> 00:01:00.809
Either way, its whole essence is ultimately
tied to an alien entity that we see take on

00:01:00.809 --> 00:01:03.710
humanoid form in the film's closing moments.

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:04.879
Through the prism

00:01:04.879 --> 00:01:08.350
Annihilation's second question is what does
the Shimmer do?

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:11.810
Determining this is the primary goal of Lena's
expedition.

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:15.810
Until her husband Kane came back, nobody who
entered the Shimmer ever returned, and he

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:20.780
seems to be sick, no longer fully in control
of himself, and clearly in pain.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:25.020
With Kane out of commission, the Area X crew
still can't say for sure what happens in the

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:29.700
Shimmer, even after throwing team after team
into its clutches… until Lena and her crew

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:30.700
journey in.

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:35.520
Despite the way our protagonists are picked
off one-by-one, the Shimmer isn't an explicitly

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:36.729
destructive force.

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:41.369
The land inside isn't a ravaged wasteland,
but a lush, exotic forest filled with surreal

00:01:41.369 --> 00:01:44.700
flora and animals that only resemble those
native to Earth.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:48.700
The scientists discover that everything exposed
to the Shimmer is in a constant, accelerated

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:53.110
state of mutation, and that mutation isn't
confined to singular DNA sets.

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:56.229
Instead, the DNA is collectively jumbled up.

00:01:56.229 --> 00:02:00.450
Animals become mixed with the plants; organic
and inorganic materials combine, connecting

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:03.570
all of nature in a very literal, very impossible
way.

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:06.040
"Do you think it's a cross-breed?"

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:10.830
"You can't cross-breed between different species."

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.200
The end times

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:15.840
It's established early on in the film that
the Shimmer is spreading.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:20.340
As the scientists journey deeper into its
confines, we see that Area X's original headquarters

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.980
has been completely overtaken by the Shimmer.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:27.050
Its threat is made abundantly clear by Jennifer
Jason Leigh's Doctor Ventress.

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:30.620
If it goes unchecked, the Shimmer will consume
the world.

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:34.830
Based on what we see, it'd be a gorgeous apocalypse
- but it's still an apocalypse.

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:38.950
While beautiful, the Shimmer is littered with
corpses and mutations, and filled with an

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:40.760
overwhelming sense of dread.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:45.099
Humans in the Shimmer encounter violent ends,
like Anya's death in the jaws of a mutant

00:02:45.099 --> 00:02:47.280
bear, or they give themselves over to it.

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:52.629
In humans, this DNA remixing leads to madness,
making them disoriented, agitated, and spaced

00:02:52.629 --> 00:02:53.629
out.

00:02:53.629 --> 00:02:57.220
The film never makes a statement on whether
the Shimmer's effects are a good or bad thing.

00:02:57.220 --> 00:03:00.520
It simply presents them as an inevitability.

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:01.790
Face-to-face

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:06.050
Toward the film's climax, Lena encounters
Doctor Ventress, who has finally made it to

00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:07.050
the Lighthouse.

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:10.680
However, Ventress has become a part of the
alien force that created the Shimmer, and

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:15.099
she soon transcends her human form and becomes
a sort of fractal prism herself.

00:03:15.099 --> 00:03:19.050
After this prism absorbs a drop of Lena's
blood, it takes on a humanoid form.

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:22.260
In this moment, Lena effectively meets the
Shimmer.

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:26.560
While it initially seems malicious, the Shimmer
never actually sets out to harm Lena.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:28.620
Instead, it just mirrors her movements.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:40.460
It's an important moment that embodies the
goals of the Shimmer, it seeks understanding

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:41.819
and integration.

00:03:41.819 --> 00:03:46.599
It assimilates to its environment; the mass
mutations and prism effect are the result.

00:03:46.599 --> 00:03:48.239
Smashing the mirror

00:03:48.239 --> 00:03:52.600
As her confrontation with the Shimmer creature
comes to a head, the creature, now in a humanoid

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:58.480
form and morphing into Lena, is given a grenade
by the real Lena: She places it in the Shimmer's

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:00.470
hands, pulls the pin, and runs.

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:05.010
As the grenade explodes, the Shimmer creature
catches fire; the lighthouse burns, destroying

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:06.780
the entirety of the Shimmer with it.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:11.129
It cements the idea that the Shimmer is one
large collective being, and also allows Lena

00:04:11.129 --> 00:04:14.799
the opportunity to escape and make her way
back to Area X.

00:04:14.799 --> 00:04:17.599
Self-destruct sequence

00:04:17.599 --> 00:04:21.119
Annihilation is a movie about destruction,
and the idea that deep in our genetic coding

00:04:21.119 --> 00:04:24.439
there's a primal urge to destroy ourselves
and the world around us.

00:04:24.439 --> 00:04:27.580
The Shimmer serves as an embodiment of that
inevitable urge.

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:31.930
It destroys what we have and turns it into
something new, for better or worse.

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:35.999
That penchant for self-destruction is explored
intensely through our protagonists.

00:04:35.999 --> 00:04:40.170
Lena is a woman who ruins her marriage with
an affair, indirectly influencing her husband

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:42.889
to go on what is potentially a one-way mission.

00:04:42.889 --> 00:04:44.460
Alma is a recovering addict.

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:46.879
Josie bears the scars of self-harm.

00:04:46.879 --> 00:04:51.300
Ventress is dying of a cancer mutating her
insides, which informs her fascination with

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:52.300
the Shimmer.

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:56.150
These characters all have a subconscious wish
to end their lives, so their journeys ever

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:59.199
deeper into the Shimmer have an air of inevitability.

00:04:59.199 --> 00:05:03.180
Even though Lena survives, she only does so
by destroying a doppelgänger of herself,

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:07.460
metaphorically wiping away her old identity
and emerging as something new.

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:09.479
Quarantine Q&amp;A

00:05:09.479 --> 00:05:13.610
Following her return from the Shimmer, Lena
is forced to take part in an extensive debriefing

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:16.389
about her journey while under a strict quarantine.

00:05:16.389 --> 00:05:18.439
Is it the real Lena or a double?

00:05:18.439 --> 00:05:21.889
After her time inside the Shimmer, the truth
is somewhere in between.

00:05:21.889 --> 00:05:26.430
After her questioning, Lena is finally reunited
with Kane, who's no longer dying from the

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:28.550
Shimmer's effects, and even seems somewhat
lucid.

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:33.360
What Lena knows, and others don't, is that
it cannot possibly be him.

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:34.889
New me, new you

00:05:34.889 --> 00:05:39.310
The most ambiguous moment of the film takes
place in its closing moments: Lena has known

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:43.110
since encountering her husband's remains at
the Lighthouse that whatever's back in the

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:46.770
Area X facility isn't him, but rather something
new.

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:51.169
Her being reunited with this Kane isn't quite
the moment those around her believe it is.

00:05:51.169 --> 00:05:55.039
She knows the truth, and needs to tie up one
last loose end.

00:05:55.039 --> 00:05:59.729
Reunited with Kane's doppelgänger, Lena asks
him if he's really her husband, and his answer

00:05:59.729 --> 00:06:00.729
is not encouraging.

00:06:00.729 --> 00:06:02.820
"I don't think so.

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:09.420
Are you Lena?"

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:13.679
Kane is something new, as well as the last
remaining fragment of the Shimmer, whether

00:06:13.679 --> 00:06:15.490
he's fully aware of it or not.

00:06:15.490 --> 00:06:19.699
In the film's haunting finale the two embrace
as both of their irises fluctuate and change

00:06:19.699 --> 00:06:24.169
color, signaling the continuing mutation and
evolution caused by the Shimmer.

00:06:24.169 --> 00:06:28.770
It now resides in Lena and Kane, who will
live on to change the world even further.

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:33.349
It might not happen soon, but the primal coding
that sends us toward self-destruction remains

00:06:33.349 --> 00:06:37.360
as an inevitability that nobody, and nothing,
will ever fully escape.

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:38.469
Thanks for watching!

